{%- comment -%}
  Crack the Cuffs — first-visit discount popup.
  Embeds the Base44 game in an iframe. Discount hand-off + code generation are
  handled entirely by the Base44 app (Shop the Drop uses Shopify's native
  /discount/{code} route via target="_top") — the theme only owns the overlay.

  - Shows once per browser via localStorage flag `crooksldn_ctc_seen`.
  - Fires ~3s after load. Append ?ctc=1 to any URL to force it (QA).
  - Closes via overlay X, backdrop tap, Esc, or the app's getaway:close message.
    The app also draws its own X inside the frame and posts the same message.
    getaway:close with target 'register' means the visitor missed and chose the
    signup instead, so we close and take them to REGISTER AS INFORMANT.

  Four things the twenty-journey audit found, fixed here. All of them are the
  overlay's fault, not the game's:

  1. FOCUS. It claimed role="dialog" aria-modal="true" and then did nothing to
     honour it — no focus move, no trap, no restore, and the close X sat after
     the iframe in DOM order, so a keyboard or screen-reader user tabbed into a
     cross-origin iframe with no announced way out (journeys 15, 16).
  2. THE ONE ATTEMPT. markSeen() fired the moment the popup opened, so anyone
     who shut it reflexively burned their only go and could never come back to
     it (18). It is now only spent on a real look — see SEEN_AFTER_MS.
  3. THE EMPTY BOX. The overlay was attached before the iframe had loaded, so
     the first 4–8 seconds were a dimmed void with nothing in it (13, 19). It
     now waits for the frame, with a timeout so a slow app still gets shown.
  4. THE COOKIE BANNER. It stacked on top of the consent banner, making the
     banner the thing you had to fight past first (02, 18, 20). It now waits
     for the banner to be answered.

  The app itself was replaced on 2026-08-20. The previous build gated the prize
  behind a phone number and then an email, and its reveal button was disabled
  while the field was empty, so pressing it did nothing at all. The current app
  asks for neither: it mints against an anonymous player id, times out after 5s
  rather than hanging, and honours prefers-reduced-motion itself.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .ctc-overlay {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 2147483647;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 16px;
    background: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.9);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
    backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }
  .ctc-overlay[data-open] {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .ctc-frame {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 440px;
    height: 90vh;
    max-height: 680px;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
  }
  .ctc-close {
    position: fixed;
    top: 12px;
    right: 14px;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 26px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: #f4f1ea;
    background: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.55);
    border: 1px solid rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.25);
    cursor: pointer;
    z-index: 2147483647;
  }
  .ctc-close:hover {
    background: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.12);
  }
  .ctc-close:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #a77ac7;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ctc-overlay {
      padding: 10px;
    }
    .ctc-frame {
      max-width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      max-height: none;
    }
    {%- comment -%}
      The app draws its own close control at the top right of its card, which on
      a phone is the full width of the screen. Ours moves left so there are not
      two overlapping tap targets. It stays rather than being removed: it is the
      one way out the parent document controls, and the only one a screen reader
      can reach without entering a cross-origin frame.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    .ctc-close {
      right: auto;
      left: 10px;
    }
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Landscape on a phone left roughly 300px of height for a 680px game, so the
    controls sat below the fold with nothing to scroll (journey 13). Give the
    frame the full height it can have and let the overlay scroll.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  @media screen and (max-height: 500px) and (orientation: landscape) {
    .ctc-overlay {
      align-items: flex-start;
      overflow-y: auto;
      padding: 8px;
    }
    .ctc-frame {
      height: 460px;
      max-height: none;
      max-width: 520px;
    }
    .ctc-close {
      top: 6px;
      right: 8px;
      width: 36px;
      height: 36px;
      font-size: 20px;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ctc-overlay {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
<script>
  (function () {
    /* The app must not send X-Frame-Options, or the browser refuses to render
       it here at all and the overlay shows an empty box. That is a per-app
       toggle in the Base44 editor: Dashboard -> Security -> settings icon ->
       Security Headers -> "Prevent Embedding", which must stay OFF. Check with
       `curl -sI <url> | grep -i x-frame-options` before changing this line. */
    var APP_URL = 'https://crackthecuffs.base44.app';
    var FLAG = 'crooksldn_ctc_seen';
    var DELAY = 3000;
    /* The one attempt is only spent once the popup has been on screen long
       enough to be a look rather than a reflex. Shut it faster than this and it
       is still waiting next time. */
    var SEEN_AFTER_MS = 8000;
    /* Consent banners, so the popup never lands on top of one. Shopify's native
       banner first; the rest are the common app banners. */
    var CONSENT = '#shopify-pc__banner, .shopify-pc__banner, #cookie-banner, .cookie-banner, [id*="cookie-consent"]';
    var CONSENT_WAIT_MS = 30000;
    var FRAME_WAIT_MS = 6000;
    var opened = false;

    function isForced() {
      try { return new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('ctc') === '1'; }
      catch (e) { return false; }
    }
    function hasSeen() {
      try { return window.localStorage.getItem(FLAG) === '1'; } catch (e) { return false; }
    }
    function markSeen() {
      try { window.localStorage.setItem(FLAG, '1'); } catch (e) {}
    }

    function consentShowing() {
      try {
        var nodes = document.querySelectorAll(CONSENT);
        for (var i = 0; i < nodes.length; i++) {
          var n = nodes[i];
          if (n.offsetParent !== null || n.getClientRects().length) return true;
        }
      } catch (e) {}
      return false;
    }

    function open() {
      if (opened) return;
      opened = true;

      var openedAt = Date.now();
      var returnFocusTo = document.activeElement;

      var overlay = document.createElement('div');
      overlay.className = 'ctc-overlay';
      overlay.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
      overlay.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
      overlay.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Crack the Cuffs');

      var closeBtn = document.createElement('button');
      closeBtn.className = 'ctc-close';
      closeBtn.type = 'button';
      closeBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Close Crack the Cuffs');
      closeBtn.innerHTML = '×';

      var frame = document.createElement('iframe');
      frame.className = 'ctc-frame';
      frame.title = 'Crack the Cuffs';
      frame.setAttribute('allow', 'clipboard-write');

      /* Close first in DOM order, so the first Tab inside the dialog reaches the
         way out rather than disappearing into a cross-origin iframe. */
      overlay.appendChild(closeBtn);
      overlay.appendChild(frame);

      /* Everything behind the dialog is hidden from assistive tech for as long
         as it is up, which is what aria-modal is supposed to mean. */
      var hidden = [];
      function hideBackground() {
        var kids = document.body.children;
        for (var i = 0; i < kids.length; i++) {
          var k = kids[i];
          if (k === overlay) continue;
          if (k.getAttribute('aria-hidden') === 'true') continue;
          k.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
          hidden.push(k);
        }
      }
      function showBackground() {
        for (var i = 0; i < hidden.length; i++) hidden[i].removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
        hidden = [];
      }

      var prevOverflow = document.documentElement.style.overflow;

      function close() {
        if (!overlay.parentNode) return;
        /* Spend the one attempt only on a real look, or when the app itself
           says the visitor is done. */
        if (Date.now() - openedAt >= SEEN_AFTER_MS) markSeen();
        overlay.parentNode.removeChild(overlay);
        showBackground();
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = prevOverflow;
        document.removeEventListener('keydown', onKey, true);
        window.removeEventListener('message', onMsg);
        if (returnFocusTo && returnFocusTo.focus) {
          try { returnFocusTo.focus(); } catch (e) {}
        }
      }

      function onKey(e) {
        if (e.key === 'Escape') { close(); return; }
        if (e.key !== 'Tab') return;
        /* Two stops inside the dialog: the close button and the iframe. Keep
           Tab between them rather than letting it walk the page behind. */
        var stops = [closeBtn, frame];
        var i = stops.indexOf(document.activeElement);
        e.preventDefault();
        var next = e.shiftKey
          ? stops[(i <= 0 ? stops.length : i) - 1]
          : stops[(i + 1) % stops.length];
        try { next.focus(); } catch (err) {}
      }

      function onMsg(e) {
        if (!e || !e.data) return;
        /* getaway:close is the current app; crooks-popup-close was the previous
           one, kept so swapping back needs no theme change.

           Deliberately NOT markSeen() on a bare close: the app posts this from
           its own X on every screen, so it means "shut this", not "finished".
           Treating it as completion would put back exactly the bug where a
           reflex close burned the one attempt. close() applies the same
           SEEN_AFTER_MS rule as every other way out. */
        var t = e.data.type;
        if (t !== 'getaway:close' && t !== 'crooks-popup-close') return;

        /* Except here. Choosing the signup after missing is real engagement,
           and it is the one hand-off the app asks us to complete. */
        if (e.data.target === 'register') {
          markSeen();
          close();
          sendToRegister();
          return;
        }
        close();
      }

      /* The popup only renders on the homepage, so the intake section is always
         on this page — no anchor or navigation needed. Focus follows the scroll
         so a keyboard or screen-reader user lands on the field, not just near it. */
      function sendToRegister() {
        var intake = document.querySelector('[data-crk-section="informant-intake"]');
        if (!intake) return;
        /* Reduced motion gets a jump, not a glide. Journey 18 rated this the
           calmest streetwear site she had used, on the strength of there being
           no animation anywhere; a smooth scroll is still an animation. */
        var calm = false;
        try {
          calm = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        } catch (err) { calm = false; }
        try {
          intake.scrollIntoView({ behavior: calm ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'start' });
        } catch (err2) {
          intake.scrollIntoView();
        }
        var field = intake.querySelector('input[type="tel"], input[type="email"], input');
        if (field && field.focus) {
          window.setTimeout(function () { try { field.focus({ preventScroll: true }); } catch (e2) {} }, 400);
        }
      }

      /* Do not show a dimmed void while the app loads. Wait for the frame, but
         never wait forever — a slow app still gets its chance. */
      var shown = false;
      function show() {
        if (shown) return;
        shown = true;
        document.body.appendChild(overlay);
        hideBackground();
        document.documentElement.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        requestAnimationFrame(function () { overlay.setAttribute('data-open', ''); });
        try { closeBtn.focus(); } catch (e) {}
      }

      frame.addEventListener('load', show);
      window.setTimeout(show, FRAME_WAIT_MS);
      frame.src = APP_URL;

      closeBtn.addEventListener('click', close);
      overlay.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === overlay) close(); });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', onKey, true);
      window.addEventListener('message', onMsg);
    }

    function whenConsentAnswered(done) {
      if (!consentShowing()) { done(); return; }
      var gaveUpAt = Date.now() + CONSENT_WAIT_MS;
      var poll = window.setInterval(function () {
        if (!consentShowing() || Date.now() > gaveUpAt) {
          window.clearInterval(poll);
          done();
        }
      }, 400);
    }

    function schedule() {
      if (isForced()) { open(); return; }
      if (hasSeen()) return;
      window.setTimeout(function () {
        whenConsentAnswered(open);
      }, DELAY);
    }

    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', schedule);
    } else {
      schedule();
    }
  })();
</script>
